# an escaped quote right before an interpolation. the literal segment ahead
# of the brace ends in `\"`, and the quote-stripper used to read that final
# quote as the string's closing delimiter — the quote vanished and the
# backslash survived, so "a\"{x}\"b" printed as a\7"b. json built this way
# was silently invalid.

fn main():
    x := 7
    print("a\"{x}\"b")
    print("{x}\"")
    print("\"{x}")
    name := "ada"
    print("{{\"sub\":\"{name}\",\"n\":{x}}}")
